{
  "tema": 6088,
  "slug": "diminutivo-illo-cillo",
  "titulo": "Diminutive -illo, -cillo, -ecillo",
  "subtitulo": "pan → panecillo, torta → tortilla, ratón → ratoncillo",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "-illo / -illa is another diminutive, built like -ito: words in -o / -a take -illo / -illa, words in -e, -n, -r take -cillo, and one-syllable words take -ecillo. In Mexico -ito is the everyday diminutive; -illo lives mostly in words with their own meaning (tortilla, bolsillo, ventanilla).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**-illo / -illa** (plural **-illos / -illas**) is a diminutive like **-ito**, and it follows the same pattern. The gender stays the same."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Word ends in",
            "Suffix",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "-o / -a",
              "-illo / -illa",
              "chico → chiquillo, campana → campanilla"
            ],
            [
              "-e, -n, -r (2+ syllables)",
              "-cillo / -cilla",
              "pobre → pobrecillo, ratón → ratoncillo"
            ],
            [
              "one syllable",
              "-ecillo / -ecilla",
              "pan → panecillo, flor → florecilla"
            ],
            [
              "pie (rare)",
              "-ececillo",
              "pie → piececillo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Same spelling changes as **-ito**: **c → qu** (chico → **chiquillo**), **z → c** (pez → **pececillo**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Mexico, **-ito** is the normal diminutive. **-illo** can sound literary, a bit pitying (**pobrecillo**) or slightly dismissive."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Many **-illo** words are now **words of their own**, with a new meaning: **torta → tortilla**, **bolsa → bolsillo** (_pocket_), **ventana → ventanilla** (_ticket window_), **cama → camilla** (_stretcher_), **cigarro → cigarrillo**, **paso → pasillo** (_hallway_)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
